⍝ AllExpressions.tc
⍝ -----------------
⍝
⍝ A structural expression fuzzer: exercises nested monadic/dyadic
⍝ application, operators, lambdas, indexing, selective/indexed
⍝ assignment, EXEC, and Quad-functions over randomly generated (but
⍝ seeded, hence reproducible) statements. Adapted from tools/apl_fuzz
⍝ (Blake McBride's crash-hunting fuzzer -- the tool behind the
⍝ Bugs27/Bugs28 "section A" reports); see apl_fuzz's own README for
⍝ the grammar and oracle design.
⍝
⍝ This file freezes one fixed-seed campaign's exact generated
⍝ statements and their real output as a standing regression check:
⍝ any statement here that starts crashing, hanging, or leaving stale
⍝ values behind is a regression. Ordinary APL errors (DOMAIN ERROR,
⍝ RANK ERROR, ...) are expected and are NOT failures -- the generator
⍝ deliberately emits "mostly legal" statements, so a good fraction
⍝ are honest errors by design. )SIC follows every statement so a
⍝ user-defined-function (lambda) failure never leaves the next
⍝ statement running inside a stale suspended state.
⍝
⍝ Deliberately NOT in Makefile.am's dist list and NOT symlinked into
⍝ testcases_3/: this is a slower, heavier check for full local
⍝ `make test` / `make test1` runs, not for `make test3` or `make dist`.
⍝
⍝ Regenerated with:
⍝   tools/apl_fuzz --seed 20260913 --count 250 --depth 3 --io 1
⍝ (apl_fuzz.cc, apl_fuzz_run -- see tools/README-apl_fuzz)

